{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1329,
    "dDurationMs": 4411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The video game Portal is a puzzle game built\naround a sci-fi device that can create a portal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5740,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "connecting one place on the wall or ceiling\nor floor to another, and portals are great"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9800,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for cooking up paradoxes and apparent paradoxes!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11600,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I already made a video about a particularly\npopular paradox (\u0026 also about how the portals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15490,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might actually work from a physics perspective),\nbut oh boy are there more interesting portal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paradoxes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21100,
    "dDurationMs": 3599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, so objects entering one end of a portal\nwith a certain speed leave the other end with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24699,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same speed, and if the portals aren’t\noriented in the same direction, then the object"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28449,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will exit in the new direction, but the speed\nwill be the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31509,
    "dDurationMs": 4681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In my first portal paradox video, I argued\nthis should apply regardless of frame of reference,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36190,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the orange portal moving towards a cube\nis the same as a cube moving towards the orange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40010,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "portal - that is, both cause the cube to shoot\nout of the blue portal with the corresponding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44070,
    "dDurationMs": 1370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relative speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45440,
    "dDurationMs": 3719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Obviously portals are fictional and there's\nno correct answer, but I think the cube shooting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49159,
    "dDurationMs": 3661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of the blue portal makes the most sense\ngiven the possible ways portals could work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52820,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "within the physics of our universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54600,
    "dDurationMs": 3989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BUT there's another paradox hiding in the\nmiddle of this one - literally."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58589,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What would happen if the orange portal stopped\nhalfway?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61550,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does the cube stay put?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62940,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does it tear itself in half?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64520,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does it shoot out of the blue portal anyway,\n\"pulling\" itself the rest of the way through?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68550,
    "dDurationMs": 1370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or something else?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69920,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'll give you a second to pause and decide\nwhat you think..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73350,
    "dDurationMs": 3670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again there's no correct answer: portals are\nfictional and you can imagine them to work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77020,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "however you like."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78470,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for physically realistic portals, I think\nthe best way to analyze the \"portal stopping"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82700,
    "dDurationMs": 5010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "halfway paradox\" is to instead imagine there\nare two cubes attached by a rope and the orange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87710,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "portal stops between the cubes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89570,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, the top cube will unequivocally\nshoot out of the blue portal at full speed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before yanking the rope taut and pulling upwards\non the bottom cube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96720,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the rope is weak then it'll break, but\nif it's strong [and if the cubes are the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99870,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mass] then it'll accelerate the bottom cube\nand slow down the top cube, so the cubes will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103370,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both shoot out of the blue portal, but at\nhalf speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106270,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if instead the orange portal stops halfway\nthrough a single cube, then if the cube is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110190,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "super fragile it should tear in half, but\nmore likely it'll just shoot out of the blue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114140,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "portal with half the speed [if the cube has\nuniform density]."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115650,
    "dDurationMs": 4149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the portal stops a third of the way through,\nthe cube'll shoot out with 1/3 the speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119799,
    "dDurationMs": 1021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Etc."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120820,
    "dDurationMs": 1089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Paradox solved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121909,
    "dDurationMs": 5371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next paradox is a bit more subtle: what\nif you try to sandwich a cube between two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127280,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "portals?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128280,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does the cube disappear?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129280,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do the portals bounce or stop?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131410,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or something else?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132670,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, I think a change of perspective is\nhelpful - imagine instead that you extend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136740,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a piston through the blue portal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138630,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Eventually it comes back and hits itself from\nbehind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140810,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The piston can't keep extending into the portal\nbecause there is no \"inside\" of the portal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144780,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- \"inside\" the blue portal is \"outside\" the\norange portal, and vice versa: everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149450,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "always exists outside the portals, and there's\nnowhere to hide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152850,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At this point one of three things could happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the piston is weak it should crumple, the\nsame as if it were pushing against a solid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158920,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159920,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the piston is rigid and the portals are\nsuper heavy, then the piston will just stop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163260,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expanding (since it can't lengthen any more\nwithout the portals moving farther apart)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167020,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the orange portal is clearly \"pushing\"\nthe piston out of it to the right, so Newton's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171550,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"equal and opposite\" law of motion means the\npiston is pushing the orange portal to the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174930,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "left - \"kind of like what happens when you\nthrow a ball\".Similarly, the blue portal is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178840,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somehow absorbing the momentum of the piston\nentering it, and so should be pushed to the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182390,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right - like what happens when you catch a\nball."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185110,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the portals aren't heavy (and aren't\non super heavy objects), then the logical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189210,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(if weird) conclusion is that the portals\nthemselves get pushed apart!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192890,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Newton's laws also apply to the paradox of\nsandwiching a cube: the blue portal moving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197400,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "towards the cube causes the cube to emerge\nfrom the orange portal like a piston, until"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201530,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the cube hits itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203090,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At which point, if the cube is weak, it will\ncrumple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205370,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If it's strong, the portals will stop or even\nget pushed apart - aka, they'll bounce!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210240,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I should say that neither of these paradoxes\nare my original ideas: the sandwich portal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214530,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paradox was sent to me by somebody who tried\nit out in a sandbox version of the portal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218310,
    "dDurationMs": 5090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "video game and got some very trippy (and non-physicsy)\nresults/glitches, and the \"halfway through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223400,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the cube\" paradox was in fact posed to me\nby the “portal physics \u0026 rendering” programmer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227580,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the team that made Portal 1 \u0026 2!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229070,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[But the solutions to the paradoxes are mine]\nApparently they thought about having moving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231300,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "portals in the game, but ended up deciding\nnot to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234440,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is lucky for us, because that means\nwe don't actually know how moving portals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237630,
    "dDurationMs": 5609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"officially\" work, and we instead get to hypothesize\nand debate and analyze portal paradoxes to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243239,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our hearts' content."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246200,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another thing you might want to debate is\nyour favorite way to draw molecules - do you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249180,
    "dDurationMs": 1639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prefer ball \u0026 stick?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250819,
    "dDurationMs": 1231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "structural formulas?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252050,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Skeletal?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253050,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ribbon diagrams?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254050,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Space-filling?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255050,
    "dDurationMs": 3070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or maybe you're into the simplicity of a lewis\ndot diagram?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258120,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whatever your preference, you can learn all\nabout the pros (\u0026 cons) of each of these molecular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262650,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "representations on Brilliant, this video's\nsponsor, where we just launched a new and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266520,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very special course created by Ever Salazar,\nMinuteEarth illustrator and molecular representation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271110,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fanatic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272110,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can I just say, I've never seen such beautiful\nmolecules, and you should definitely go check"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276129,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277129,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which you can!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278129,
    "dDurationMs": 3391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can sign up for Brilliant for free at\nBrilliant.org/minutephysics, and the first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281520,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "200 people will get 20% off an annual Premium\nsubscription with full access to all of Brilliant’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286340,
    "dDurationMs": 3499,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "courses and puzzles, including our molecule\ndrawing course!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289839,
    "dDurationMs": 3711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, that's Brilliant.org/MinutePhysics\n- and thanks to Brilliant for letting us take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293550,
    "dDurationMs": 989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over one of their courses."
    } ]
  } ]
}
